    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, as the code actually runs.\n\n## Pre-controller (Spring framework, before the method body)\n\n1. **Security authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`. Caller must hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`, else 403.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (declared on the generated `OwnersApi` interface). All constraints are checked before the method runs; any failure \u2192 400. Constraints:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` (optional): `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` (optional): `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - `registrationDate` (optional): `@Valid`\n   - `sharesHousehold` (optional): no constraints\n\n   (The `Owner`/`Person` entity constraints \u2014 `@NotEmpty`, telephone `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`, `@Email` \u2014 are **not** re-validated on this path; no `@Valid` on the entity.)\n\n## Inside the controller method, in this exact order\n\n3. **normalizeAddress** \u2014 mutates `address` in place: trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand ST\u2192STREET / RD\u2192ROAD / AVE\u2192AVENUE. This normalized value is what gets stored and used downstream.\n4. **rejectBlankOwnerFields** \u2014 manual re-check that `firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone` are non-null and non-blank \u2192 400 if any missing.\n5. **rejectInvalidPostcode** \u2014 `PostcodeValidator`: null is allowed; otherwise 4 digits and, for a recognized region (NSW/VIC/QLD ranges via `LocalityResolver`), within range \u2192 400 on failure.\n6. **normalizeTelephone** \u2014 canonicalizes to E.164 (strip separators, keep `+CC` or assume `+61` dropping a leading `0`; enforce 8\u201315 digits and exact national length for known country codes) and **writes it back**; invalid \u2192 400.\n7. **normalizeEmail** \u2014 if present, trim, regex-validate, lowercase, and **write back**; invalid \u2192 400. (Blank/null left as-is.)\n8. **compute householdId** \u2014 SHA-256 hex of normalized `lastName\\naddress`.\n9. **rejectDuplicateIdentity** \u2014 loads **all** owners; despite building a telephone|email|household key, it actually rejects only on a **telephone** comparison-key collision \u2192 409.\n10. **rejectCityAtCapacity** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); `>= 50` \u2192 409.\n11. **effectiveRegistrationDate** \u2014 supplied date or `now()`, then rolled to a business day (Sat\u2192+2, Sun\u2192+1).\n12. **countRegisteredOn** \u2014 counts existing owners with that adjusted registration date.\n13. **rejectDailyRegistrationLimitReached** \u2014 if that count `>= 100` \u2192 429.\n\n## Building and persisting the entity (side-effects)\n\n14. **map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`): copies firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone, email, registrationDate, postcode; id and pets ignored.\n15. **set derived fields on the entity:**\n    - `registrationDate` = business-day-adjusted date\n    - `householdId` = the computed hash\n    - `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive)\n    - `bulkSignupWarning` = `registeredThatDay > 80`\n    - `householdSize` = existing members of that household + 1\n16. **saveOwner** (`ClinicServiceImpl`, `@Transactional`):\n    - if new and no customer code, **generate `customerCode`** = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN = (count of existing owners in that city) + 1, zero-padded (reads all owners again).\n    - **persist** via repository (`em.persist`; pets would cascade via `CascadeType.ALL` but none exist on create).\n17. **AUDIT log** \u2014 logger `\"AUDIT\"` emits `owner created id=... customerCode=... registrationDate=...`.\n18. **map entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`** \u2014 computes response-only derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `locality`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`).\n19. **set `Location` header** to `/api/owners/{id}` and **return 201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notably absent\nNo custom `ConstraintValidator`s (the \"custom\" rules are imperative util classes), no `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/`@EntityListeners`, no password encoding, no events, no emails/messaging. Id is DB-generated (`IDENTITY`).\n\nOne correctness flag worth surfacing: step 9's method name and key-building imply a telephone+email+household uniqueness check, but it only actually enforces **telephone** uniqueness \u2014 the email and household components never participate in the match."
  },
